WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:08.320
SCP-682 Vs Y-909. Can the compound derived&nbsp;
from SCP-3000, the legendary Ananatashesha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.400
be the thing that finally ends&nbsp;
the wretched life of SCP-682?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.680
Y-909 is the key ingredient&nbsp;
in Foundation amnestics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.000
and the researchers discovered a curious&nbsp;
thing when it was added to 682’s tank:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.560
It caused an increase in the damage that&nbsp;
hydrochloric acid did to the creature’s body.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.040
This suggested that 682’s regenerative&nbsp;
abilities are somehow tied to its memories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:35.920
of previous damage taken. Some researchers&nbsp;
proposed taking SCP-682 directly to SCP-3000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.440
to see if the giant eel could&nbsp;
kill 682 once and for all.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.240
However, this proposal was soundly rejected,&nbsp;
due to too many unpredictable factors:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:49.760
From the risk of transporting 682, to its&nbsp;
unpredictable adaptive response to SCP-3000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:55.360
such as it possibly growing to SCP-3000’s&nbsp;
insane size or stealing its amnestic abilities.

